package example;

import example.dto.BookView;
import org.babyfish.jimmer.sql.JSqlClient;
import org.babyfish.jimmer.sql.ast.Page;
import org.babyfish.jimmer.sql.ast.mutation.SaveMode;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class CanaryJava {

    private CanaryJava() {}

    public static BookView create(JSqlClient sql, String name, BigDecimal price, String tenantId) {
        Book input = Immutables.createBook(draft -> {
            draft.setName(name);
            draft.setPrice(price);
            draft.setTenantId(tenantId);
            // store omitted -> null; no association touched
        });
        return sql.saveCommand(input)
                .setMode(SaveMode.INSERT_ONLY)
                .execute(BookView.class)   // follow-up fetch, returns the full view
                .getModifiedView();
    }

    public static Page<BookView> search(JSqlClient sql, String name, int page, int size) {
        BookTable b = Tables.BOOK_TABLE;
        return sql.createQuery(b)
                .where(b.name().likeIf(name))                 // predicate skipped when name == null
                .orderBy(b.name().asc(), b.id().asc())        // id tie-breaker = stable paging
                .select(b.fetch(BookView.class))
                .fetchPage(page, size);                       // pageIndex is 0-based
    }
}
```

**Duplicate name:** `INSERT_ONLY` never upserts. The insert hits the database unique index backing `@Key`/`@KeyUniqueConstraint`, and Jimmer surfaces it as a `SaveException` (constraint violation) unless the project's exception translator maps it; nothing is updated and no partial view is returned. `@Key` is save-matching metadata — the real enforcement is the DB uniqueness, so test it on the actual dialect.

**Create success:** there is no acceptance flag. `isModified` is *not* persistence success. Because the method returns the view directly, the contract is: normal return (non-null view with generated `id`) = insert executed; otherwise it throws. If explicit row evidence is required, keep the `SimpleSaveResult` and check `getAffectedRowCount(Book.class)` (zero is meaningful).

Remaining check: compile via the project's APT build; the two coordinate-sensitive spots are the `org.babyfish.jimmer.sql.ast.Page` import and the `execute(BookView.class)` overload. Add when needed: a duplicate-name integration test against the real schema.
